---
title: Sesame Soy Pork Bowls
servings: 2
prep time: 5 min
cook time: 20 min
source: HelloFresh recipe card, "Sesame Soy Pork Bowls with Sriracha Mayo, Cilantro & Crispy Onions" (WK 29-3)
---

Add @jasmine rice{3/4%cup}, @water{1 1/4%cup}, and a pinch of @kosher salt{} to a #small pot{}. Bring to a boil, cover, reduce to a low simmer, and cook for ~{15-18%minutes}, until the rice is tender. Keep covered off the heat until serving.

Zest and halve the @lime{}. Roughly chop the @cilantro{1/4%oz}. In a #small bowl{}, combine @mayonnaise{2%tbsp} and @sriracha{1%tsp}.

Heat @cooking oil{1%tsp} in a #large pan{} over medium-high heat. Add @ground pork{10%oz} and a generous pinch of @kosher salt{}. Cook for ~{4-5%minutes}, breaking the pork into pieces, until browned.

Stir in @shredded carrots{4%oz}, @sweet soy glaze{2%tbsp}, and @sugar{1/2%tsp}. Cook for ~{2-4%minutes}, until the carrots soften, the pork is cooked through, and the sauce has thickened. Season with @kosher salt{} and @black pepper{} to taste.

Fluff the rice with a #fork{}, then stir in the lime zest and @butter{1%tbsp}. Season with @kosher salt{} and @black pepper{} to taste. Divide the rice between bowls and top with the pork mixture and any sauce remaining in the pan. Drizzle with the sriracha mayo, then sprinkle with the cilantro and @crispy fried onions{1.5%oz}. Serve with lime wedges.
